        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0411" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.34537/113.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 571.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 27, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s instruction
                    (No. 170) of the 21st ultimo, I have the honor to transmit herewith the
                    agreement amending the agreements between the United States and Cuba concluded
                    February 16/23, 1903, and July 2, 1903, by which certain areas of land and water
                    in Guantánamo and Bahía Honda were leased to the United States for coaling and
                    naval stations. This agreement was signed by me to-day on behalf of the United
                    States and by Señor Manuel Sanguily y Garritt, Secretary of State, on behalf of
                    the Republic of Cuba.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d421-a1.xml" xpointer="d421-a1"/>
